2. Material under other terms
-----------------------------

2.1 Title music: public/dawnbreakers.m4a

    "Dawnbreakers", by macattacka, made with Suno (https://suno.com).

    This recording is NOT covered by the MIT or Apache licenses, and no
    license to it is granted by this repository. Its use is governed by
    Suno's Terms of Service for the account that created it. If you
    redistribute or adapt the game, remove or replace this file unless you
    have the rights to it. The game falls back to its own synthesized dawn
    theme (part 1) when the file is absent.

2.2 Quoted scripture and narrative

    The dialogue and story text are original, dramatised paraphrases of
    Nabil's narrative. A few short passages are quoted word for word from
    Shoghi Effendi's English translations in "The Dawn-Breakers: Nabil's
    Narrative of the Early Days of the Baha'i Revelation" (1932), which
    remain under the copyright of their rights holders and are quoted here
    for the purpose of telling the history. They are NOT relicensed under
    part 1. They are:

      * Tahirih's verse "The effulgence of the Abha Beauty hath pierced the
        veil of night..." (src/data/dialogues_ch/qazvin_karbila.ts)
      * Vahid's prayer in the words of the Imam Husayn, "Thou knowest, O my
        Beloved..." (src/data/dialogues_ch/nayriz_end.ts)
      * the verse of the Qur'an (37:180) rendered "far be the glory of thy
        Lord, the Lord of all greatness, from what they impute to Him"
        (src/data/dialogues_ch/trial_court.ts)
      * the chant of the Siyah-Chal, "God is sufficient unto me; He verily
        is the All-Sufficing!" and "In Him let the trusting trust."
        (src/data/dialogues_ch/chapter10_siyah_chal.ts,
        src/data/dialogues_ch/chapter10_exile_road.ts,
        src/data/story/chapter10.ts)

    The Persian and Arabic originals of these passages are in the public
    domain.

2.3 Star catalogue: data/sky/hipparcos.csv, src/data/travelStars.ts

    Derived from the Hipparcos Main Catalogue: ESA, 1997, "The Hipparcos
    and Tycho Catalogues", ESA SP-1200, as distributed by the CDS,
    Strasbourg, as catalogue I/239
    (https://cdsarc.cds.unistra.fr/viz-bin/cat/I/239). This research has
    made use of the VizieR catalogue access tool, CDS, Strasbourg, France
    (DOI: 10.26093/cds/vizier). The data are used under the CDS and ESA
    conditions of use, which ask for this acknowledgement; keep it with
    any copy.

2.4 Map geography: src/data/glossary/mapData.ts

    Derived from Natural Earth (https://www.naturalearthdata.com), which is
    in the public domain. Made with Natural Earth.

2.5 Phaser and the libraries bundled into the built game

    The built game includes Phaser 3 (MIT, Copyright (c) 2024 Richard Davey,
    Phaser Studio Inc.) and eventemitter3 (MIT, Copyright (c) 2014 Arnout
    Kazemier). Each build writes their full license texts to LICENSE.txt
    next to index.html, generated from the packages actually bundled.

    patches/phaser+3.90.0.patch changes Phaser's source; the Phaser code in
    it is under Phaser's MIT license, and the changes are under part 1.

2.6 Native Sky Rewind (native/skyrewind-cpp)

    Its build downloads GLFW 3.4 (zlib/libpng license,
    https://github.com/glfw/glfw) and Dear ImGui 1.90.9 (MIT,
    https://github.com/ocornut/imgui). Neither is stored in this repository.
    A binary of the native app built from them must carry their notices.

2.7 Development tools

    The packages installed only for development (Vite, TypeScript, ESLint,
    Playwright and the rest of package.json's devDependencies) are not
    distributed with the game and remain under their own licenses.
